WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.797
Hugging Face pipeline is the easiest way to experience a pretrained task model.

00:00:06.797 --> 00:00:10.992
In the example, pipeline receives the task name sentiment-analysis.

00:00:10.992 --> 00:00:17.477
The library loads an appropriate model and tokenizer, prepares the text, runs inference,

00:00:17.477 --> 00:00:24.922
and formats the result. You pass in an ordinary sentence and receive a label with a confidence score.

00:00:24.922 --> 00:00:32.347
That convenience is excellent for demonstrations and quick baselines because it hides a lot of boilerplate.

00:00:32.347 --> 00:00:39.787
The tradeoff is that you have less visibility into tokenization, tensors, logits, batching,

00:00:39.787 --> 00:00:45.672
and device placement. Start with pipeline when you want to verify that a task works.

00:00:45.672 --> 00:00:53.622
Move to AutoTokenizer and a task-specific AutoModel class when you need more control, custom preprocessing,

00:00:53.622 --> 00:00:58.572
batching, fine-tuning, or access to intermediate outputs.

00:00:58.572 --> 00:01:04.707
Run the code, then replace the sentence with one that is ambiguous or domain-specific and see how the

00:01:04.707 --> 00:01:06.718
prediction changes.
